#{[17592186391149 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c4/c497d1f9dd6cb5bc473bd46ec56c465228408447fb2436b80f16a23b282654b2.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391149 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391149 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9fcceae6-4fa4-5965-9386-71fc659c0936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391150 #edb/ref 1080 "images/4f/4f613e414cdb619a9b09f25a47b7e4cad953440c40d91f876322d7e1cb59b8c4.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391150 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391150 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "65324022-a078-5bdb-b4aa-e0381dbb7e37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-5y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7685d561-af7c-5963-8ff0-5f1c98ad02e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391169 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ with the eigenvector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-4t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on the $x$-axis and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5$ with the eigenvector $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-5t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on the $y$-axis and also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/b4/b406c864e820819c5ae6f548c7a025a1e1d8197fb785ea5689080034e04210cb.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186391171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391170 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e78979b2-0930-5c53-983d-999f23a46873" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391171 #edb/ref 1080 "a stable node (sink)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391171 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391171 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "461def2d-f65b-5702-81dc-9c688ad9792a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391172 #edb/ref 1080 "a saddle point" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391172 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391172 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64590024-0b5d-5509-b3ed-cec5555ef505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391173 #edb/ref 1080 "an unstable node (source)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186